WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.100
Data is modern industry's
most powerful asset,

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.030
but raw numbers are useless
without the skills to decode them.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.700
National University's Fundamentals
of analytics course

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.590
is your step-by-step gateway
to building those solutions.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.500
It starts with structured data,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.230
highly organized tabular information
in rows and columns.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.500
This requires completely
different handling

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.150
than the chaotic, unformatted scope
of unstructured or big data.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.780
Once your data is structured,
you need to understand its shape.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.020
We measure its central tendency
by locating the mean, median and mode.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.060
Then we measure how far that data
spreads to find its standard deviation.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.220
But professional data science isn't
just about looking at single variables.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.860
By analyzing covariation, we use simple
linear regression to predict interactions.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.000
Next, you bring this math to life
using industry-standard tools

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.500
like R programming and ggplot2.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.500
By mastering how to structure, measure,
model and visualize data,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:03.140
you build the analytical toolkit
required to solve complex problems.